# Normalize line endings. Shell scripts MUST stay LF or they break on the Linux CI runner
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not a valid interpreter path).
*.sh    text eol=lf

# C# is pinned to LF on checkout (not just normalized in the index). `dotnet format` is a
# blocking CI stage that runs on the Linux runner where the working tree is LF; without an
# explicit eol here, `core.autocrlf=true` checks C# out as CRLF on Windows and `dotnet format`
# (which follows .editorconfig's `end_of_line = lf`) then rewrites every file. Pinning eol=lf
# makes local and CI agree. The determinism gate is unaffected — the golden hash is computed
# from GameState, never from source bytes. See EF-003 and `.editorconfig`.
*.cs    text eol=lf

# JSON/YAML/Markdown stay text with auto line-ending on checkout (deliberately not pinned).
*.csproj text
*.json  text
*.yml   text
*.md    text
*.asmdef text
*.slnx  text

# Desync captures under evidence/ are raw wire bytes. These MUST stay byte-exact — the whole
# point of the file is that its hash is reproducible, and `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would
# silently rewrite CR/LF pairs inside the payload and invalidate the evidence.
*.frame binary
